# LF in every checkout, whatever the machine's core.autocrlf says.
# Vite copies the manifests and HTML entries byte for byte, so a CRLF
# checkout on Windows produced packages that differed from the CI
# (Linux) release build in line endings — and the AMO 1.3.0 upload was
# such a local build. With this, any OS rebuilds the same bytes.
* text=auto eol=lf
*.png binary
*.zip binary

# Keep the AMO source-review zip (git archive) lean: screenshots are
# listing assets, not build inputs — they were ~6 MB of an 8.5 MB zip.
docs/screenshots/ export-ignore
